[1mNAME[0m
    demo - exercise every roffsub
    element

[1mSYNOPSIS[0m
    [1mdemo[0m [[1m-r[0m] [[1m-k[0m [4mlist[0m] [[4mfile[0m ...]

[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
    [1mdemo[0m reads each [4mfile[0m in turn, or the
    standard input when none is named,
    and writes the records it finds in
    the order chosen by the options. A
    space written as a backslash space,
    as in a b c, never breaks. Fonts may
    change mid word, as in [1msrt[0m(1) and
    [4mfile[0m.txt.

    A second paragraph follows the first
    after one blank line, and it is long
    enough to wrap at every width the
    reference outputs use, which is the
    point of it.

[1mOPTIONS[0m
    [1m-r[0m  reverse the emitted order.

    [1m-k[0m [4mlist[0m
        sort by the columns in [4mlist[0m,
        then the remaining columns in
        order.

    [1m--respect-blanks[0m
        treat each indented block as a
        unit; the tag is longer than the
        indent, so the body starts on
        the next line.

    [1m-x[0m  a width of four sets the
        prevailing indent, which the
        next item keeps.

    [1m-o[0m[4m file[0m
        write to [4mfile[0m instead of the
        standard output.

  [1mLists[0m
    o   bullets use the bullet
        character, shown as o on an
        ASCII terminal.

    o   a second bullet item.

    1.  a numbered item with its own
        width.

    2.  a second numbered item.

  [1mNesting[0m
    Text before a nested block.
        Nested text sits one prevailing
        indent further in.
           A deeper block, moved in by
           three cells.
        Back at the first level.
    Back at the section margin.
    After a line break, still the same
    paragraph.


    After two blank lines.

[1mTABLE[0m
     [1mOPTION[0m   [1mMEANING[0m
    --------+-------------------
     [1m-r[0m       reverse the order
     [1m-k[0m [4mKEY[0m   sort on [4mKEY[0m

    A boxed table with a text block:
    -------+---------------------+------
     [1mNAME[0m    [1mDESCRIPTION[0m           [1mSIZE[0m
    -------+---------------------+------
     alpha   a long description      12
             that has to wrap
             when the terminal
             is narrow, kept
             inside its column
     beta    short                 3456
    -------+---------------------+------

[1mEXAMPLES[0m
    demo -k5,3 file
    demo -r < input > output

[1mSEE ALSO[0m
    [1msrt[0m(1), [1mroffsub[0m(7)
